{"ref":"BDB, דָּחַף","hw":"דָּחַף","html":"† <big><big>[<span dir=\"rtl\">דָּחַף</span>]</big></big>  <strong>vb. drive, hasten</strong> (late) <strong>(</strong>NH <em>id.</em>, Aramaic <span dir=\"rtl\">דְּחַף</span><strong>)</strong>—<br><strong>Qal</strong>  <em>Pt.</em> pass. pl. <span dir=\"rtl\">דְּחוּפִים</span> of runners <a data-ref=\"Esther 3:15\" href=\"/Esther.3.15\">Est 3:15</a>; <a data-ref=\"Esther 8:14\" href=\"/Esther.8.14\">8:14</a> (‖ <span dir=\"rtl\">מְבֹהָלִים</span>).<br><strong>Niph.</strong>  Pf. <em>hasten one’s self, hurry</em> <span dir=\"rtl\">נִדְחַף אֶל־</span> <a data-ref=\"Esther 6:12\" href=\"/Esther.6.12\">Est 6:12</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">נִדְחַף לָצֵאת</span> <a data-ref=\"II Chronicles 26:20\" href=\"/II_Chronicles.26.20\">2 Ch 26:20</a> (‖ <span dir=\"rtl\">בהל</span>).","next":"BDB, מַדְחֵפָה","prev":"BDB, דֹּ֫חַן"}